# Bibliography Deep Dive

## Executive Summary — Bibliography
This research monograph provides a master bibliography for the **Technological Singularity** research library within the **Convergence** macro-historical framework. Replacing generic template appendices, it compiles 35+ peer-reviewed academic papers, foundational books, technical alignment monographs, and empirical benchmark reports across computer science, AI safety theory, macroeconomics, semiconductor physics, and global governance (Amodei et al., 2016; Bostrom, 2014; Christiano et al., 2018; Elhage et al., 2021; Hubinger et al., 2019; Kurzweil, 2005; Russell, 2019; Vinge, 1993; Yudkowsky, 2008).


| Primary Domain | Foundational Authors | Target Analytical Focus |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1. Singularity & ASI | Vinge, Good, Bostrom, | Intelligence explosion, event horizon |
| Theoretical Roots | Kurzweil, Moravec | & pathways to superintelligence |
| 2. AI Alignment & | Yudkowsky, Christiano, | Interpretability, mesa-optimizers, |
| Technical Safety | Amodei, Elhage, Hubinger | scalable oversight, outer/inner align |
| 3. Compute Scaling & | Sevilla, Erdil, Kaplan, | FLOP datasets, scaling laws, |
| Hardware Physics | Hoffmann, Landauer | algorithmic progress halving rates |
| 4. Macroeconomics & | Nordhaus, Hanson, | Capital-labor substitution, Baumol |
| Governance Policy | Acemoglu, Dafoe, Shavit | cost disease, compute caps, IAIA |


